  "decisions": [
    "Transfer reviewed data through the existing SDK source APIs, never by copying undocumented SQLite state. Exact app/workspace provenance, SDK note revision/digest, native source content and producer identity must all agree.",
    "New cache keys bind the exact producer. Import preserves original creation and only shortens expiry, requires fresh source admission, and never restores old contexts, principals, grants or handoffs.",
    "Durable bounded generations use a separate owner HMAC role, three-generation limit, protected key/path/lock checks and request/snapshot idempotency. They do not select or enable CIGAR.",
    "After SDK-write/native-ack interruption, recovery verifies actual SDK revision/provenance and completes the native commit without replaying SDK mutation. Imported preparation text is removed.",
    "Reverse preparation starts from current reviewed data so removed notes are not resurrected. This data primitive is not yet an integrated runtime rollback.",
    "Existing native retention and explicit Forget saved data cover generations while disabled. Missing keys/corrupt records can be explicitly cleared without silently provisioning new trust."
  ],
  "development_corrections": [
    "Visibility staging briefly changed method parameters; exact original method bodies were restored before compiling. Staging exact-match failures made no writes.",
    "Actual fixture API and ownership errors were corrected before the successful run. Clippy findings were resolved using inspect_err, exact chunks and a boxed entry, without suppression.",
    "Explicit forgetting initially left a lock-only root classified as unavailable; existing() now recognizes that empty namespace and the native disabled-state regression passes.",
    "Read-only process inspection is unavailable inside this sandbox; approved read-only inspection outside it returned no remaining CIGAR worker/broker."
